{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/492716-baseline-tech-and-iron-man-nova","id":492716,"title":"Baseline tech and \"iron man\" nova","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-26T10:37:31-07:00","id":492716,"title":"Baseline tech and \"iron man\" nova","content":"The new Aberrant timeline will be set around 2028 so the baseline tech aided by nova genius will be advanced with i suppose things like drones, powered armor, laser etc. (btw the previous edition nailed some real world advances) how this will be integrated with gadgets build by novas, in setting not mechanically? There will be a gear list in the core book of advanced but not &quot;inspired&quot; tech for those who like to play a batman like character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T17:42:41-07:00","id":493053,"title":"","content":"I often marvel a little at the prescience of the timeline in the Aberrant core. Even guessing the name selected by the new Pope in the 2000's.<br /> <br /> That said, given the &quot;the world if...&quot; nature of the older game line, I'd be a little surprised if we didn't see plenty of snapshots of technological advancements and how they impact the lives of baselines and novas alike. The focus of Aberrant will undoubtedly be the novas themselves, but it would probably be easy enough to adapt the rules there and in the TC core to make a Batman-style character (arguably a fine example of a daredevil), if the rules don't come standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T18:09:04-07:00","id":494179,"title":"","content":"I found it silly that they had a sidebar called &quot;No, you can't be Iron Man&quot; in the section where they showed you how to be Iron Man. Sure, it would take awhile to do but the rules fully allowed you to make a suit or armor and pilot it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T19:13:21-07:00","id":494225,"title":"","content":"The Aberrant Player's Guide, between that sidebar and the infamous &quot;This is Not the Super-Friends&quot; introduction, was an uncharacteristic collection of useful information with a smattering of &quot;You are having badwrongfun with our game, shame on you&quot; blurbs. That was not likely the intention behind those segments (at least I hope not), but this did make a bit of a stain on the game line. From what we've seen, however, they're not likely to repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:33:27-07:00","id":495373,"title":"","content":"Badwrongfun chiding was part of the time, and much like heavy handed metaplots it's really something the writers have left behind. You get occasional preachy soapboxes now and then, but nothing nearly as bad. Honestly there were a few times over the years I suspected the authors actively hated the player base and just felt we were holding them back. Probably the biggest sing of change is that Aberrant will be compatible with Scion, so it would be literally possible to play Thor.<br /> <br /> With any luck the new system will include something like Adventure's invention system that can cross all three lines, because hey, maybe I want to develop new biotech too, and be Iron Man, and laugh maniacally on my zepplin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T17:15:01-07:00","id":495450,"title":"","content":"With my players, I shudder at the thought of crossing Aberrant with Scion. I already have them riding up the side of buildings and then playing pogo-katana on the zombies heads. Now toss in things like being Raiden? Oh hell no. I turn in my ST screen at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T17:44:49-07:00","id":495488,"title":"","content":"To each his own, really, which is part (there are so many parts...) of my excitement for the new edition. The freedom to do what you will within the &quot;Sardonyx&quot; games means there is no badwrongfun outside of what you decide at the table. If you want to run Thor fighting Titanspawn alongside the Avengers, you can. If the idea drives you mad, skip it. Personally, I'm all for Raiden defending Earthrealm alongside Caestus Pax, but I can't blame anyone for wanting to avoid it.<br /> <br /> More on topic, one of the bits that tweaked me about the original Aberrant was the inconsistency of mega-mental types. You had brilliant novas curing terminal illnesses like an Olympian clearing hurdles, turning Ethiopia into paradise on Earth, creating an engine that far outstrips anything mankind had created in terms of efficiency... But Iron Man or detecting &quot;Hey, there's something weird in my meds...&quot; were kind of hand-waved or shouted down. I suspect this will be less of an issue, and I'm grateful for it.<br /> <br /> Oh, speaking of engines, look up Audi's new e-diesel concepts for some ideas for how the hyper combustion engine of the future might need to evolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}